{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.KummerUnitCircle","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.KummerUnitCircle","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerLobachevsky","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Arg"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Kummer.tetAngles_exp_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Kummer.tetAngles_exp_sum","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerUnitCircle.lean#L196-L203","doc":"The angles really do sum to `π`, as `tetAngles_sum_eq_pi` requires — recorded\nas an independent check that the three computations above are mutually\nconsistent rather than three separate slips. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Kummer.blochWigner_lob_exp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Kummer.blochWigner_lob_exp","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerUnitCircle.lean#L178-L194","doc":"**KUMMER'S IDENTITY ON THE UNIT CIRCLE.**\n\nFor `θ ∈ (0, π)`, the Bloch–Wigner Λ-sum at `z = e^{iθ}` is `Cl₂(θ)`.\n\nThe tetrahedron is *isosceles* — angles `(θ, (π−θ)/2, (π−θ)/2)` — and the\nidentity is exactly Clausen duplication.\n\n⚠ This is the Λ-side only, and only on `|z| = 1`.  It makes no claim about\n`Im Li₂` — for that, and for the two halves combined, see\n`QOU/Knot/KummerDilogHalf.lean`.  Neither reaches the 5₂ shape, which has\n`|y₁| = 1.52`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Kummer.Lob_add_two_Lob","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Kummer.Lob_add_two_Lob","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerUnitCircle.lean#L167-L176","doc":"**The Λ-identity behind it**: `Λ(θ) + 2Λ((π−θ)/2) = Cl₂(θ)`.\n\nImmediate from `Cl_2_duplication`, since `Λ(t) = Cl₂(2t)/2`:\n`Cl₂(2θ)/2 + Cl₂(π−θ) = Cl₂(θ)` is the duplication formula halved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Kummer.tetAngle₃_exp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Kummer.tetAngle₃_exp","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerUnitCircle.lean#L151-L163","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Kummer.tetAngle₂_exp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Kummer.tetAngle₂_exp","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerUnitCircle.lean#L142-L149","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Kummer.tetAngle₁_exp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Kummer.tetAngle₁_exp","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerUnitCircle.lean#L138-L140","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Kummer.arg_one_sub_exp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Kummer.arg_one_sub_exp","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerUnitCircle.lean#L126-L134","doc":"`arg (1 − e^{iθ}) = (θ − π)/2` for `θ ∈ (0, π)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Kummer.one_sub_exp_mul_I","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Kummer.one_sub_exp_mul_I","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerUnitCircle.lean#L100-L124","doc":"**The half-angle factorisation.**  `1 − e^{iθ} = 2 sin(θ/2) · e^{i(θ−π)/2}`.\n\nThis is the whole geometric content: the modulus `2 sin(θ/2)` is positive on\n`(0, 2π)` and the phase `(θ−π)/2` lands in `(−π/2, 0)`, so the argument of\n`1 − e^{iθ}` is `(θ−π)/2` on the nose, with no branch ambiguity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.Kummer.arg_exp_mul_I","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.Kummer.arg_exp_mul_I","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerUnitCircle.lean#L94-L98","doc":"`arg (e^{iθ}) = θ` on `(−π, π]`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}